    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d616">

                <pb facs="0630" n="624" xml:id="pg624"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851B.20/36a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General in Martinique (Malige)</hi><anchor n="78" xml:id="d616-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-08T20:00:00-04:00">May 8, 1942—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>92. The French Embassy was requested today to advise Admiral Robert that Admiral
                        Hoover<anchor n="79" xml:id="d616-f2"/> and Mr. Reber<anchor n="80"
                        xml:id="d616-f3"/> are scheduled to arrive at Fort-de-France tomorrow
                    morning, Saturday, May 9, by plane from Puerto Rico for consultation with the
                    High Commissioner.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d616-f1" n="78" type="source" xml:id="d616-f1-content">
                <p>On April 10, 1942, Mr. Malige was promoted from Consul to Consul General in
                    Martinique.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d616-f2" n="79" xml:id="d616-f2-content">
                <p>Adm. John H. Hoover, U.S. Commander of the Caribbean Sea Front.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d616-f3" n="80" xml:id="d616-f3-content">
                <p>Samuel Reber of the Division of European Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
